Falsifies `file_allocation_table::master_boot_record::verification::every_sector_parses_to_a_sound_table_or_an_error`.

The defect: the end check allows a partition to end up to sector 2^33, so an entry whose first sector
and length add past the 32-bit sector numbers is accepted, and the device would add its first sector
to an index it then cannot name.

Expected to fail: the harness's assertion that a partition ends within 2^32.

diff --git a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/master_boot_record.rs b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/master_boot_record.rs
--- a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/master_boot_record.rs
+++ b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/master_boot_record.rs
@@ -171,7 +171,7 @@ impl MasterBootRecord {
             if sectors == 0 {
                 return Err(MasterBootRecordError::EmptyPartition { index });
             }
-            if u64::from(first_sector) + u64::from(sectors) > 1 << 32 {
+            if u64::from(first_sector) + u64::from(sectors) > 1 << 33 {
                 return Err(MasterBootRecordError::PartitionOverflows { index });
             }
             *slot = Some(Partition {
